      {
        "id": "253e7fc5-b914-4c7b-aacf-fad12bf82f83",
        "name": "Sorter Notes",
        "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
        "typeVersion": 1,
        "position": [
          0,
          -160
        ],
        "parameters": {
          "color": 4,
          "width": 1700,
          "height": 300,
          "content": "## Sorter (C2 #29, C3 #30)\n\nEvery minute: load `automation/streams.json` from oneshotllc/.github once, then loop RPOP `queue:intake` (max 500/run).\n\n**Triage path** (not yet seen): route repo → stream from the table, LPUSH to `queue:<stream>`. The consumer posts the spec, labels `hold`, sets `spec:{key}`.\n\n**Approval path** (already seen): if the item is an issue (not a PR), has no `hold` label, and `spec:{key}` exists, INCR `build:{key}`; on the first claim only, LPUSH to `queue:build:<stream>`. Removing `hold` on GitHub is therefore the one approval action; the next poller tick (≤5 min) releases the build exactly once.\n\nNo model calls here, ever. Table lookups and Redis keys only."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "b080a0d1-bff7-43ca-bc0b-0d4139dd2079",
        "name": "Approval Eligibility",
        "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
        "typeVersion": 2,
        "position": [
          1320,
          -140
        ],
        "parameters": {
          "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
          "language": "javaScript",
          "jsCode": "// Approval path (C3, oneshotllc/.github#30): a seen issue with no `hold` label may proceed to the build queue.\nconst src = $('Pop Intake Item').item.json.item;\nconst labels = (src.labels || []).map(l => typeof l === 'string' ? l : (l && l.name) || '');\nconst isPR = /\\/pull\\/\\d+/.test(String(src.issue_url || ''));\nconst held = labels.includes('hold');\nconst key = `${src.repository_owner}/${src.repository_name}#${src.issue_number}`;\nreturn { json: { key, eligible: !held && !isPR, held, isPR } };"
        }
      },
